  "stem": "A particle moving in the xy-plane experiences a velocity dependent force $\\overrightarrow{F} = k(v_{y}\\widehat{i} + v_{x}\\widehat{j})$, where $v_{x}$ and $v_{y}$ are x and y components of velocity. If $\\overrightarrow{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle, then which of the following statements is true for the particle?",
  "options": {
    "A": "Quantity $\\overrightarrow{v} \\times \\overrightarrow{a}$ is constant in time",
    "B": "$\\overrightarrow{F}$ arises due to magnetic field",
    "C": "Kinetic energy is constant in time",
    "D": "Quantity $\\overrightarrow{v}.\\overrightarrow{a}$ is constant in time"
  },
  "answer": {
    "keys": [
      "A"
    ]
  },
